I am sitting by the table.
A worker comes to me.
He has a small tray in his hand.
He places it on the table.
My iced tea and banana cake are on it.
"Here is the tea and cake," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say happily.
He goes back.
I take the iced tea.
The glass is very cold.
I slowly drink it.
It is very good in this heat.
Then I eat the banana cake.
The cake is very sweet.
I look outside through the window.
The road outside is very busy.
Vehicles are going fast.
But I feel very peaceful here.
